## 🎁 Lucky Gift Boxes

Possible rewards included movement boosts, shields, double jump, event currency, and temporary buffs.

## 🌨️ Visibility / Movement Disruption

Snow Storm effects could reduce visibility and make navigation harder.

## 🔔 Counter-Power Idea

Santa Bell could disable Giant powers for 10 seconds.

This supports the broader GIANTBOUND idea that Tiny Players should have ways to interrupt or counter Giant abilities.

## 🦌 Reindeer Assist

Could provide a shortcut, speed boost, bridge repair, or event currency.

This can inspire future support or utility systems.

## 🚫 Buddy Rescue

The old concept contained a Buddy Rescue system with temporary team-wide buffs. It is not part of the current GIANTBOUND direction unless it is redesigned for a future mode.

## ⚔️ Original Win System

The old concept used Yeti HP reaching 0 as the Survivor win condition and time expiration as the Yeti win condition.

This structure is now specifically associated with the planned **Classic Mode** foundation, while future GIANTBOUND modes can use different objectives.

## 🏆 Original Rewards

The old concept included coins, XP, Buddy XP, gift tokens, Christmas stars, candy canes, achievements, and event progress.

GIANTBOUND can reuse the useful reward philosophy while creating its own economy, levels, cosmetics, and progression.

## 🔗 How This Connects to GIANTBOUND

The complete source pool can feed Classic Mode, including:

- 🪤 Giant environmental control
- ⚡ Giant temporary powers
- 💰 Limited Giant resource spending
- 🧰 Tiny temporary upgrades
- 🧗 Parkour and moving traversal hazards
- 🎁 Lucky temporary rewards
- 🌨️ Visibility and movement disruption
- 🔔 Counter-power concepts
- 🦌 Support/utility concepts
- 💥 Cannon-based objective gameplay
- ❤️ Short respawn

The goal is to preserve the strongest parts of the original game while integrating them into GIANTBOUND's larger lobby, map, mode, customization, and reward systems.
